  "description": "spec 06 section 4.2 — re-submitting a request nobody has answered. Given the requests a component `held` and the `call` it is about to gate at `now`, `expected.resubmit` is the `request-hash` it MUST resolve to and `expected.decided` the answered request it MUST consume instead; `null` means it MUST park the request under `minted`. Identity is the nine fields of `call`, never `request-hash` — `minted.request-hash` differs from every held hash in every vector, which is what `nonce` (section 1.1) is for. A held request is eligible only while `state` is `pending` and `now` has not passed its `not-after`.",
